---
type: agent/instruction
description: Hand an existing linked worktree to a fresh agent session
usage: "guide://_worktree/use/<worktree-name>"
minargs: 1
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
includes:
  - ../_partials/handoff-context-target
---
Using the current Git worktree inventory, read {{>handoff-context-target}}.
Locate the `worktrees.{{args.0.value}}` entry
and use its recorded `path`, task metadata, phase, plan, and instructions as the
child handoff. Do not alter unrelated top-level entries or worktree entries.

Give the child the worktree name `{{args.0.value}}` and its recorded path. Do not
forward this session ID. The child must report its working directory, create a
fresh Guide interaction, bind the shared project root and that worktree, then
read the shared handoff context before proceeding.
